border-*-style: double. A double side three pixels or wider paints two lines and the gap between them, as Chromium paints it
(box_border_painter.cc, BorderEdge::GetDoubleBorderStripeWidths): the outer line (w + 1) / 3 wide at the outer edge, the inner
one from (2w + 1) / 3 to the inner edge, in whole pixels, each line a ring of its own whose corners follow the border's radii
less its offset; a narrower double side is solid. A side of another style beside a double one is all outer line.
CSS Backgrounds 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-backgrounds-3/#border-style

